{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n[`Criterion::Ok`](../../../rustdocs/trust_but_verify/graph/trait.Criterion.html#associatedtype.Ok)\ndefines the criterion's completed answer:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse serde::{Serialize, de::DeserializeOwned};\n\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// The completed answer, including any negative assessment.\n    /// Its Serde JSON representation must reconstruct the completed answer.\n    type Ok: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate for `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait.answer`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. `Criterion::Ok` is bounded by `Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send`.\n2. The answer type can carry a negative assessment as a completed answer.\n3. The answer's Serde JSON representation reconstructs the completed answer.\n\n**Mapping to tests**\n- **Negative answers and the JSON round trip.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` uses a `Review<Answer>` criterion with `satisfied: false` and details \"missing edge case\". The `Answer` struct derives `Serialize` and `Deserialize`.\n  - It asserts that `verify` returns the negative output unchanged.\n  - After `store_evidence`, it asserts that the stored record's `output` is exactly `json!({\"satisfied\":false,\"details\":[...]})`. That checks the JSON representation.\n  - It then asserts that `load_evidence` returns an output equal to the original `negative`, both through `output()` and `into_output()`. That checks reconstruction.\n  - It repeats the round trip for a `Vec<String>` answer and for a unit `()` answer, whose stored output is `json!(null)`. This varies the shape of the answer type.\n- **`Send` without `Sync`.** `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` in the same file uses a `Cell<u32>` answer. `Cell<u32>` is `Send` but not `Sync`.\n  - It runs `verify`, `store_evidence`, `load_evidence` and `refresh_evidence` through a `send(...)` helper and asserts the round-tripped value is 17.\n  - This exercises the `Send`-only bound and shows that serialization and deserialization work for such a type.\n- **End-to-end negative answer.** `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk]` stores a negative agent answer (`determination` false).\n  - It asserts that the record's `output` equals the answer and that the cached load returns an equal answer.\n  - It uses a real SDK criterion whose `Ok` type is `serde_json::Value`.\n- **Trait bounds.** The `Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send` bounds are compile-time constraints. Every test criterion has to satisfy them to compile, so the compiler enforces them.\n\n**Gaps**\nI found no untested obligation, assertion gap or marking gap. All three tests carry `{test}` references to the subject. There are no acknowledgments and none are needed.",
